              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for gladly, then the Telugu for the body."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: మన్నించండి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మన్నించండి (manniñcaṇḍi) — \"please pardon me\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It does the work of క్షమించండి, and is the gentler, native word beside it. Either answers a mistake; మన్నించండి (manniñcaṇḍi) is the one to use with an elder."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A second apology, softer than the first."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
